    ],
    "modules": {
      "src/main.tsx": "Mounts Preact and starts local project restoration/autosave.",
      "src/ui/App.tsx": "Four active tabs (Single cable, Load list, Cable sizing, Drums), undo/redo controls with global Ctrl/⌘+Z handling, keyboard-shortcut sheet, project name, backup controls, toast messages and the print-only Report root. Includes the light/dark theme toggle. The project dialog (project-name button) renames the project and offers \"Start a new project\" with a confirm step.",
      "src/ui/state.ts": "Signals, computed single/list/drum results, input mutations, whole-project undo/redo history (300 steps, typing in one cell within 1 s is one step, not persisted), load-list view state (filter, search, selection, inspected row), debounced tab-scoped autosave and explicit erasure. Also holds the light/dark theme signal (default light, stored in localStorage). fresh() is a neutral empty workspace named \"Untitled project\"; newProject() replaces the project with it in one undoable step and resets the load-list view state.",
      "src/ui/SingleCable.tsx": "One unchanged workbook row, result strip, missing-input shortcuts, inline Calculation panel (pick a size from the ladder), print/PDF and Excel export.",
      "src/ui/LoadList.tsx": "Import mapping dialog; header with Import menu (load list or schematic), Add row, a More menu (Print / PDF, Ask AI) and Export to Excel as the only primary action; one-line summary (status split, connected load on final circuits only, worst total VD opening its calculation, cable km toggling quantities with drum links, pending suggestions with Accept all); one filter bar (panel dropdown, status chips, search, issues list with jump-to-cell, Defaults popover for suggestion settings, View menu with screen-only column presets plus the colour key); bulk edit of selected rows, grid, calculation drawer and 'How the sheet works' notes. Appending enforces the 2,000-row project limit. Drop routing by file type, reading progress bar with Cancel, and the schematic review dialog.",
      "src/ui/Sheet.tsx": "Grid of the workbook's 72 columns (A–BT) with workbook colours, dropdowns, Excel keys (Enter, arrows at text edges, Ctrl/⌘+D fill down, Delete clears dropdowns), row selection on the Item cell, optional filtered row order, calculation/delete row tools, block paste and virtualization above 60 visible rows. Optional screen-only column groups (GROUPS: a group row above the letters, hiding unpicked groups; A–D stay pinned) and per-row status marks on the Item cell.",
      "src/engine/sheet.ts": "Pure workbook-equivalent formulas and dependent lists. CALC_COLS has 33 columns; INPUT_COLS has 39 (ITEM_COLS, the original 23, drive Item numbering). Numeric comparisons follow 15 significant digits. RowResult.helpers exposes the step05 helper columns (keys AT–AY, workbook BY–CD since step09) and helpers.fault (earthing system, nominal U0, transformer Z, Ze, Ia, IΔn, CPC type/k/multiplier/size/resistance, Ik, times, energies, final circuit). Earth fault loop for TN-S and TT with RCDs and CPC (AP–BG) and short circuit (BH–BO) via faultCells, chained from the feeding row (Ze ← Zs BB, TT only from a TT row; fault level ← BM); CHECK_COLS/failsCheck list every PASS/FAIL column (AG, AN, BE, BG, BJ, BO, BT). Motor starting VD (step09 BP–BT): BR = AL + (multiple − 1) × AK with the multiple typed (BQ) or the starter type's value on Lists (TABLES.starters), checked against BS or Settings Def_StartVD (15 %).",
      "src/engine/suggest.ts": "Preliminary suggestions for protection, list-default cable/cores/method/VD and size/parallel sets. Settles upstream rows first.",
      "src/engine/procurement.ts": "Groups valid rated products and expands parallel/physical cable runs. Single-core quantities count 3 per three-phase set or 2 per single-phase set; neutral and earth are excluded. Flags groups whose electrical checks are incomplete or fail.",
      "src/engine/drums.ts": "Pure layer/turn geometry, bend-radius and payload/lift constraints, per-run allowance and first-fit decreasing allocation.",
      "src/engine/result.ts": "Typed success/error union for recoverable engine results.",
      "src/import/load-list.ts": "ExcelJS read-only workbook import, CSV/TSV parser, header aliases, explicit unit cleanup, mapping and drum-template parsing. Ambiguous numbers remain invalid instead of being partially parsed.",
      "src/import/document.ts": "Local PDF text extraction with position-aware columns, drawn table borders for equipment datasheet pages (rulesOf), and on-device PaddleOCR for scanned pages (ocrReader loads ONNX Runtime and the models from vendor/ocr/; imagePixels). Used by supplier drum imports and the catalogue datasheet reader. Equipment datasheet pages' text is built by phrases; cable catalogues keep item-by-item text.",
      "src/import/ocr.ts": "On-device PaddleOCR PP-OCRv5 mobile through ONNX Runtime Web (wasm; threads when the page is cross-origin isolated): DB text-line detection, a reader picked per page (Latin, Cyrillic or Chinese) by its confidence on the widest lines, greedy CTC decoding, each line read whole and its words shared out over its printed parts by length (parts found from ink, grid lines ignored). Models live in models/paddleocr (Apache-2.0, commits and hashes pinned).",
      "src/import/drum-catalogue.ts": "Supplier drum CSV/XLSX import or explicitly labelled/unit-qualified PDF/image text extraction. Candidate values require review before activation.",
      "src/import/parse.ts": "Delimited text and cable-field extraction helpers shared with document reading, ocrLines (OCR word boxes to positioned lines in page points, so scanned rating tables are read like typed PDFs), and rulesOf (table borders and shaded cells from pdf.js's operator list, in page points); electrical catalogue UI is archived. pdfLines turns pdf.js text items into positioned lines (shared by the app and the bench); phrases writes an equipment page's text as an engineer reads it: items a word space apart (judged by letter width) joined, wide gaps, drawn borders and dotted leaders parting columns.",
      "src/export/template.ts": "Patches only entered input cells in the original XLSX ZIP, retains all formulas/validations/styles, extends beyond 196 rows and adds preview caches.",
      "src/store/schema.ts": "Zod version-2 project, worksheet rows, cable geometry and drum library schemas. Some document-reading schemas remain for supplier extraction. Project carries sheetLayout 8; a project without it is migrated once by LEGACY_FAULT (step06 and step07 fault input letters to their step08 columns). Loads.learned: labels taught in the review (equipment type id, parameter key, label), at most 500.",
      "src/store/project.ts": "Tab-scoped sessionStorage autosave and erasure, targeted cleanup of legacy IndexedDB project keys, validated backup import and browser downloads.",
      "src/ui/Drums.tsx": "Linked or typed runs, geometry confirmation, adaptor controls, allocation cards and enquiry export.",
      "src/ui/DrumSources.tsx": "Supplier file chooser, extraction progress, review acknowledgement and basic/supplier selection.",
      "src/ui/DrumVisual.tsx": "Code-native SVG drum on a continuous turntable rotation (28 s per turn) with convex-hull cylinder outlines and near/far flange draw order that flips with the angle. Drag to turn; stays still for prefers-reduced-motion and pauses off screen. Visual fill is illustrative.",
      "src/ui/components.tsx": "Shared form, badge, notice, metric and number-format components.",
      "src/ui/app.css": "Token-based theme: light warm-paper/graphite/safety-orange default and a graphite dark theme under :root[data-theme=dark], workbook legend tokens for sheet headers, dashboard/drawer/calculation/drum styles and @media print report styles. All screen colours are CSS variables; older unused selectors remain from the rebuild.",
      "src/data/sizing-tables.json": "Generated lookup data: 67 columns (A–BO), 3,260 ratings in 461 blocks, 27 temperature rows, 100 grouping keys and 7 soil rows. Also the FaultData tables (Cu resistance, k values, resistance multipliers, device multiples, transformer Uz) and the Settings defaults Ze, fault level, clearance time and Cmin. Plus the CPC type table (k, resistance multipliers, same-material and IEC 60228 flags) and the SS 638 Table 41.1 disconnection times (TN-S and TT), the earthing system list and the default earthing system.",
      "scripts/extract-workbook.mjs": "Extracts workbook tables for the 67 app columns A–BO (validations of visible columns, all Settings notes, the FaultData sheet incl. CPC types, TN-S/TT disconnection times and the earthing list, and Settings defaults incl. Def_Earthing) and copies the unmodified template; checks contiguous lookup blocks.",
      "scripts/build.mjs": "esbuild IIFE build, vendored assets/fonts, checksums, file watching and loopback static server. Each build verifies the approved release file list, the blank workbook and pinned runtime assets. Unexpected files and links prevent publishing. The loopback server also sends no-referrer, frame-ancestors none/X-Frame-Options DENY, COOP/CORP same-origin, COEP require-corp (cross-origin isolation lets the OCR use threads) and a restrictive Permissions-Policy.",
      "scripts/verify-vendor.mjs": "Verifies the release file list and compares the blank workbook and bundled PDF, OCR and font assets with reviewed SHA-256 pins.",
      "scripts/dkg.mjs": "Generates this graph, code/import/export index, file hashes, change history and stale-check commands. Watches project files during dev.",
      "scripts/verify.mjs": "Runs the full check sequence, records results against a source fingerprint and refreshes the DKG.",
      "src/ui/Calculation.tsx": "Hand-calculation view of one row (Ib, k factors, minimum It, Iz, circuit and total VD), size ladder with pick buttons and the From→To feeder chain. Display only; values come from sheet.ts.",
      "src/ui/Report.tsx": "Print-only A3 landscape report (schedule with suggested values marked, KPIs, cable quantities, open issues, Prepared/Checked/Approved block). Uses window.print; the browser saves PDF locally.",
      "src/engine/explain.ts": "sizeLadder evaluates every size of the row's rating block through evaluateRow with the same current/VD tests as column AB; feederChain follows first-match From→To links. No independent maths.",
      "src/engine/issues.ts": "Derives errors (invalid cells, current/VD FAIL), warnings (None passes, Out of range, duplicate To tags, total-VD chain breaks) and info (missing inputs) from calculated rows. Cell references use Excel row numbers.",
      "src/import/guard.ts": "Pre-parse guards: XLSX ZIP central-directory size/entry limits (checkZip) and image header dimensions (imageSize/checkImage, 12,000 px side / 60 MP) before any decoder runs; used by load-list, schematic and drum/catalogue imports.",
      "src/import/schematic.ts": "Pure, deterministic schematic-to-load-list engine (no AI). DXF parser (TEXT/MTEXT/ATTRIB, binary/size guards, bounded MTEXT clean-up), glyph/word merging on shared baselines, readFacts (breaker A, poles/phase, kW/HP/W/kVA, PF, diversity, voltage incl. 400/230 pairs but not cable insulation ratings, cable type/cores/size/sets, run length, tags, board names, fed-from/feeds-to, spares, title-block words), circuit-schedule table detection (reuses detectColumns/toSheetRows plus cell rescue), single-line-diagram grouping around breaker ratings for column or row layouts with a proximity fallback, board ownership, From→To feeder chain, deduplication across drawings, inferred values with reasons, and limits (100k text items, 20k per page, 4k breakers per page, 200 pages, 2,000 candidates). Traced line work (from images or rendered PDF pages) gives one row per feeder: the busbar label (board tag first, within 7 text heights above or 15 left of its start) is From for drops and To for incomers; labels attach to the nearest feeder by distance from the nearest part of the text, with the far end counting 4 text heights closer and vertical text along the feeder preferred for the load name. Also reads US/MV notation (6-1/C 500 → 1C, 500 kcmil, 2 sets; 3/0 AWG; ft and miles to metres; MW, MVA), ETAP-style tags (TR:4, 3WTR:1, Bus A), transformer ratings into B, and treats a bare C16 as an MCB rating only on pages that mention MCBs or amps.",
      "src/import/schematic-read.ts": "Browser reader for schematics: pdf.js text with page rotation and text direction, PaddleOCR for pages without a text layer or for images, UTF-8/Windows-1252 DXF decoding, cancel support, 25 MB/page/text-item limits, image header dimension check before decoding, friendly pdf.js and DWG messages. Images and scanned PDF pages go through drawing-ocr (scale up to 2x for small screenshots, 24 MP working budget); vector PDF pages are rendered to trace busbars and feeders under the text layer. Returns the text read for the review.",
      "src/ui/Schematic.tsx": "Review dialog for circuits read from a schematic: tick/untick rows, page and source text per row, worked-out values in italics with their reason, notes (spares skipped, unsupported voltages, DC, unticked fed-from feeders), Create load list / Add to current list. Opens even when no circuits are recognised, explaining why and showing the text that was read; a collapsible \"Text read from the drawing\" panel is always available.",
      "src/import/raster.ts": "Pure image helpers for drawings (plain RGBA arrays, linear in pixels): luminance, Otsu threshold, ink mask, line mask that ignores strongly coloured mark-ups, straight-stroke detection with thickness, quarter-turn rotation and mapping of rotated word boxes, and feeder tracing: busbars are long horizontal strokes with feeders (two if heavier than other long lines, else three; twice-bent cable routes rejected), feeders are followed through bends and across symbol gaps (breakers, fuses, coils) using an endpoint grid. Limits: 8,000 strokes, 60 busbars, 1,500 feeders.",
      "src/import/drawing-ocr.ts": "Image pipeline shared by browser and tests: OCR of the page as drawn (PaddleOCR reads text among line work; erasing lines cut letters) in three orientations (upright, upward, downward text) with tiling for large sheets (each word kept from the tile that owns its centre), noise filter for short words, lone capitals kept only after an adjacent word of similar height, de-duplication of words read twice, then busbar/feeder tracing with text masked. The OCR engine is injected. Also tokenBox, traceLines (vector PDF pages) and scaleGeometry.",
      "src/engine/loads.ts": "Equipment-list engine: row and catalogue shapes, catalogue index and fill (Brand + Model + Configuration), per-row kW/kVAr/load factor, panel and plant totals with operating factors and design margin, and the scenario comparison.",
      "src/import/equipment.ts": "Equipment-list workbook import (panel sheets, brand catalogue sheets, factors and margin, view-sheet and heading-row skipping), catalogue/panel merging, Send to cable sizing mapping and merge, and datasheet proposals from PDF/OCR text or a local model reply with per-value page verification. Proposal.doubt holds the parameters whose values do not add up with each other and the sums worked out (checks.ts).",
      "src/export/equipment.ts": "Load list Excel export: a cover page, then one sheet per panel laid out cell for cell as the engineer's designed panel sheet (equipment-layout.ts) with live formulas; catalogue-only export.",
      "src/ui/Loads.tsx": "Load list tab: panel tabs, the equipment grid (ticks, dropdowns, catalogue placeholders, Excel paste), panel totals with editable factors and margin, import, export and Send to cable sizing.",
      "src/ui/Catalogue.tsx": "Brand catalogue view: editable entries, brand filter and search, workbook import, export, and the datasheet review dialog (text/OCR or local AI, red unverified values, only-rows-to-check filter, page view with a box round each value read, tick to add; blank models and repeated model + configuration refused). Paste web page dialog (clipboard HTML) and .html files through Read datasheet. Amber cells for values that do not add up (checks.ts), rechecked on every edit. In the page view a parameter can be picked and its value clicked: the row takes it and the label printed before it is learned for that equipment type (project loads.learned; Forget learned labels clears them, Undo restores).",
      "src/ui/Scenario.tsx": "Search across panels by KKS/description, scenario comparison table and inline-SVG grouped bar charts, plant load by panel.",
      "src/export/equipment-layout.ts": "Panel sheet layout: header rows 1-6, at least 32 item rows, the running plant load, operating factors and load basis summary, page setup; formulas with cached results.",
      "src/import/vocabulary.ts": "Rating-table field vocabulary as data: words for kW, current, voltage, efficiency, power factor, speed, poles, type/series names, part codes, frame sizes and not-load-data columns in English, German, French, Spanish, Italian, Portuguese, Dutch, Polish, Turkish, Russian and Chinese, plus symbols and units matched as printed; fieldsIn scores a heading line (longest phrase first, abbreviations by prefix). nameScore matches any equipment type's parameter to a printed label three ways: by the quantity both name in any vocabulary word (Rated power for Rated output, FLA for Rated current) with every other word printed, by the parameter's own words (fuzzy OSA distance for OCR slips, bracketed words optional), or by a symbol printed (In, Ue, Icu; another symbol of the same quantity rejects); units must agree. namesQuantity, unitNames (kvar, kVA, lm name their quantity alone) and users' own units serve the readers. Words printed for one another (HV/high, LV/low, Specs/standard) are alike; a load point (75 % load, full load) is not part of a name while no-load stays one word; what follows \"at\" in a printed label is its condition and never makes it another parameter. A label the engineer taught by clicking its value (Param.labels) names its parameter before any other route.",
      "src/import/rating-table.ts": "Columns are named by vocabulary.ts in any listed language, checked against their values, and found from P = √3·U·I·η·cosφ when no heading is understood; type/series name = model, row-distinguishing code (product ID, frame) = configuration, title product name for size-only tables. Catalogue rating tables (one row per motor/pump/fan) read by column position from PDF item x/width: columns from overlapping numbers, stacked headings classified bottom-up (kW, hp, In at 400 V, efficiency/power factor at full load; starting current, torque, weight skipped), poles from speed or sub-headings, voltage/Hz/phase from the heading context. Rows are checked against P = √3·U·I·η·cosφ (In/Un flagged when they do not add up); a name column repeated down the table goes into the configuration, and every value keeps its page box for the review's page view. Drawn borders (rulesOf) keep a heading inside its own cell and stop values joining a column across a border. A load-point column (100 %, 75 %, 4/4) that no heading names takes its neighbour's efficiency or power-factor field, so a heading centred over 75 % still yields full-load values. With equipment types picked (catalogueFromTables types), each table is read for the type whose ticked parameters its columns give most: feedsOf gives every load-list-feeding parameter its column by nameScore (one column each, best first, efficiency/pf at full load only), else the vocabulary/P-formula column of the one quantity its label names; a table needs two parameters with columns and half the required ones, so breaker, DB, capacitor and other non-motor tables are read and motor-only rules apply only without types.",
      "src/import/webpage.ts": "Vendor product web pages pasted from the browser or saved as .html: HTML to text (regex, never rendered), label/value pairs and comparison tables to catalogue proposals, HP to kW, checked with verify. Also reads PDF datasheets laid out as label/value columns (catalogueFromDatasheet): long labels match by their known start only with the field's unit, signal inputs and losses skipped, ligatures and wrapped labels rejoined, brand from label, title or copyright. With equipment types picked, a one-product sheet or page is read for each type (paramsOf: every ticked parameter, feeding or not, takes its best-named label, one value each, best first, full load preferred, part load only when the parameter is named at it, a unit like kvar printed once names its parameter, running-text lines split by looseOf); the product takes the type found most and its load list columns come only from that type's parameters, in the column's unit (W and hp as kW). A label split by a symbol in another font (\"Efficiency (\", \"ɳ\", \") at 100% Load\") is rejoined at its brackets; a power in kVA or kvar is never kW; columns the chosen type does not fill are cleared; each value read is boxed where it is printed (placeOn: the item on the line after its label). Lines are read with the section heading printed over them (HV side, Losses). Two labels naming a parameter equally with different values are settled by the row's sums (checks.ts). pickAt reads a value clicked in the review's page view and the label printed before it; placeOn boxes a value printed as several items.",
      "src/import/checks.ts": "An engineer's arithmetic on a datasheet row (checkRow): a kVA rating over √3·U gives each side's current, kW over √3·U·cosφ (·η for shaft output) gives a load's current, kVA over kVA plus no-load and load losses gives efficiency at power factor 1 or 0.8, and a load's protection is at least its current. Sides (HV/LV, primary/secondary, input/output) come from parameter names; phases from the row or its Phases parameter, a supply above 250 V being three-phase. A relation that fails flags its values as doubt with the sum; withCheck and checkAll apply it to review rows; withTypes uses it to choose between tied values.",
      "src/engine/equipment-types.ts": "Equipment types as data: built-in list (motor to HV and MV transformers) and the user's own, each parameter feeding a load list column or kept with the entry only; pickedTypes, defaultOn, doubleFeeds. withLearned adds the labels the engineer taught (Param.labels) to the picked types before a read.",
      "scripts/bench.mjs": "Private accuracy bench for the catalogue reader: bundles the reader for Node, reads each PDF in a folder (default samples/bench, ignored by git and deployment) exactly as the app does, and scores it against the engineer's confirmed <name>.json (types, pages, rows of expected values), per sheet and per parameter, also listing rows that do not add up. --draft <types> writes a starting <name>.json from the values read. Scanned pages are not benched."
    },
    "calculationReference": {
      "electrical": "I1 = kW × diversity × 1000 / (V × PF × (sqrt(3) for 3-phase, else 1)); Ib = I1 × sqrt(1 + THD²); Iz = It × parallel × Ca × Cg × Cs × Ci × Ct; circuit VD% = Ib × run_m × mV/A/m / (10 × parallel × V).",
      "suggestedSize": "Preserves original workbook row-order/count-failing-candidates formula. Source ratings are ordered contiguous blocks; do not replace it independently of Excel parity.",
      "upstream": "Total VD uses the first To matching From. Blank From gives blank total VD. A nonblank unmatched From is a supply boundary with zero upstream VD.",
      "drum": "layers=floor((flange-2clearance-barrel)/(2OD)); turns=floor(width/OD); geometric_m=pi*turns*(layers*barrel+OD*layers²)/1000; capacity=min(supplier_override_or_geometric*fill, min(payload,lift-tare)*1000/kg_per_km).",
      "earthFaultLoop": "TN-S and TT, SS 638:2018 / IEC 60364 (step08 AP-BG). Earthing system per row (AP, blank = Settings Def_Earthing TN-S). U0 = nominal (V/sqrt3 rounded to 10 V for 3-ph, V for 1-ph). Required disconnection time = SS 638 Table 41.1 by system and U0 for final circuits (In <= 32 A, To feeds no row): TN-S 0.8/0.4/0.2/0.1 s, TT 0.3/0.2/0.07/0.04 s; else TN-S 5 s (411.3.2.3L), TT 1 s (411.3.2.4L). R1+R2 = (r20 phase x m phase + r20 CPC x m CPC) x run / (1000 x parallel). Zs = Ze + R1+R2 (TT Ze typed or from a TT feeding row). Max = larger of the overcurrent limit (TN-S Cmin x U0 / Ia, 411.4.5L; TT 50 / Ia, 411.5.4L) and the RCD limit 50 / IDn (TN-S 411.4.5L, TT 411.5.3L / Table 41.5). Check: TN-S Zs <= max; TT Ra (typed) or Zs <= max. Ia = 5/10/20 x In for MCB B/C/D or typed. If = U0/Zs. CPC: Table 54.2 minimum; PASS by selection when CPC >= minimum, else adiabatic (k2 x S x n)^2 >= If^2 x t. Computed by the app (faultCells) and checked against tests/fixtures/excel-fault-crosscheck.json (165 circuits).",
      "shortCircuit": "IEC 60364-4-43:2023 431.5.4 (step08 BH-BO): breaking capacity >= fault level at From (431.5.4.1). I2t = typed let-through or (Ik_from x 1000)^2 x t; min size = sqrt(I2t)/(k x parallel), k from 4-43 Table 2 (115/103 PVC, 143 XLPE); PASS when size >= min, else FAIL, or 'Check let-through' for an MCB row with no let-through (431.5.4.2: below 0.1 s the device let-through applies). Ik_to = Ik_from / sqrt(1 + (m x r20 x run/(1000 x parallel) x Ik_from x 1000 / U0)^2), m 1 (3-ph) or 2 (1-ph). Computed by the app and checked against tests/fixtures/excel-fault-crosscheck.json (165 circuits)."
    },
    "dataContracts": {
      "projectVersion": 2,
      "projectKey": "spool-project-v2",
      "worksheet": "Record of input column letters to strings; derived results are recomputed.",
      "physicalDimensions": "OD in mm, cable mass in kg/km, minimum bend radius as a multiple of OD.",
      "drumDimensions": "Flange/barrel/winding width/clearance in mm; payload/tare/lift in kg; allowance in percent.",
      "limits": {
        "loadRows": 2000,
        "fileMB": 25,
        "workbookSheets": 30,
        "worksheetRows": 10000,
        "worksheetColumns": 200,
        "pdfPages": 200,
        "drumOptions": 100,
        "drumRuns": 2000,
        "xlsxUncompressedMB": 200,
        "xlsxZipEntries": 5000,
        "undoSteps": 300,
        "csvRows": 10000,
        "csvColumns": 200,
        "cellChars": 300,
        "schematicTextItems": 100000,
        "schematicTextItemsPerPage": 20000,
        "schematicBreakersPerPage": 4000,
        "schematicPages": 200,
        "schematicCandidates": 2000,
        "imageSidePx": 12000,
        "imageMegapixels": 60,
        "dxfLines": 12000000
      },
      "migration": "Older device autosaves (IndexedDB) are deleted on start, not restored. Earlier circuit/catalogue models are not silently converted."
    },
    "knownLimits": [
      "Electrical calculations reproduce the supplied workbook; a PASS covers its current-capacity and voltage-drop checks, not a complete certified installation design.",
      "Stored fixture provenance says Microsoft Excel recalculated 260 rows on 2026-10-28. Regression tests compare those recorded values; they do not launch Excel on every run.",
      "Imported XLSX formulas use saved results, which can be stale. The UI asks engineers to recalculate/save the source before import.",
      "Duplicate To tags retain the workbook's first-match semantics. Engineers must resolve ambiguous network names; cycles cannot provide a meaningful total VD.",
      "The original workbook's underground grouping table repeats factors beyond six circuits. These are preserved for parity and require engineering validation for the actual arrangement.",
      "No automatic cable diameter, mass or bend-radius inference from cross-section. Dimensions must match the exact product and be confirmed for each selected group.",
      "Single-core run counts omit neutral and earth. Add separately when their product/size differs or plan explicit typed runs when extra conductors are required.",
      "Supplier PDF/OCR extraction handles explicitly labelled units, not arbitrary unlabeled tabulations. Use reviewed CSV/XLSX or manual adaptor inputs when extraction is incomplete.",
      "No cable-catalogue/IEC electrical workflow, authentication, multi-user revisions, purchase orders, cloud backend or published site is active in this version.",
      "Browser session restore can retain work. Save a JSON backup for deliberate long-term storage.",
      "Undo history is lost on reload. Use JSON backups for checkpoints.",
      "Print/PDF relies on the browser print dialog; choose A3 landscape and enable background graphics for PASS/FAIL shading.",
      "Duplicated or restored tabs can hold separate copies. Clear this tab’s data removes its autosave and undo history. Exported files are ordinary files on the device.",
      "A real HTTPS deployment still needs response-header, artifact, injected-script and host-log review. See docs/security-review.md.",
      "The drum turntable animates with requestAnimationFrame, so browsers pause it in hidden tabs or panes.",
      "Schematic recognition is rule-based. It reads text, not line work: connections are inferred from where annotations sit (around each breaker rating, in schedule tables or in CAD block attributes). Unusual layouts can group text wrongly, so the review step is mandatory reading. Tags are taken as written; differently spelt board names (MSB1 vs MSB-1) are not linked.",
      "Image reading (screenshots, scans, PDFs without a text layer) uses on-device OCR in three orientations plus line tracing of busbars and feeders. It handles orthogonal single-line diagrams; diagonal lines, dense overlapping labels, red-line mark-ups over text and very small text (under about 10 px) read poorly. Numbers from OCR must be checked in the review.",
      "DWG is not readable; export ASCII DXF or PDF. Binary DXF and block-definition text other than attributes are not read. AWG/kcmil sizes, DC systems and voltages outside the workbook list are kept but cannot be sized by the workbook.",
      "The workbook ratings cover LV cables (230–690 V). Medium/high-voltage drawings (e.g. 13.8 kV, 138 kV) are read and listed with their drawing voltage, but rows show as invalid on the sheet until MV rating tables are supplied.",
      "Earth fault loop, RCD, CPC and short-circuit columns AP-BO cover TN-S and TT only (SS 638:2018, IEC 60364). Ze and fault level default to blank (not assumed); a TT row needs Ze typed or a TT feeding row. Not modelled: TN-C, TN-C-S and IT systems, cable reactance (Zs reads low above about 35 mm2), the IEC 60909 voltage factor c and minimum fault currents, RCD discrimination, the TN-S times allowed for a bonded TT installation on an overcurrent device, electrode stability above 200 ohms, Annex A.3 exemptions, fuse Zs tables (type Ia). A separate copper CPC is taken as PVC-insulated and not bunched; armour and tape need catalogue area and resistance.",
      "Load list: the export's intermittent reactive operating-factor formula intentionally follows the supplied template, which can differ from the app's total-load calculation. The panel sheet matches the designed \"Panel 1\" cell for cell (except the KKS heading); it has not been opened in Excel here, so the print preview is unchecked. Text placeholders in consumed load, efficiency or power factor are left out of the export. Scenario inputs are not saved; the In vs Ib check is not run on send; one header block per sheet is read on import; the equipment grid has no arrow-key navigation.",
      "Datasheet checks cover only kVA–voltage–current, kW–voltage–current–power factor–efficiency, losses–efficiency and protection against current; a wrong value that still adds up, or one in a relation missing a value, is not caught.",
      "Learned labels apply per equipment type and exact printed label (spaces and case aside), on single-sheet label/value reading only, not per brand and not to rating-table headings.",
      "The accuracy bench reads PDF text layers. Private keys may match configurations by named fields. Missing products earn no field credit. The importer reads product-column tables, explicit full-load internal battery runtimes, printed motor frame codes, split ratio subscripts and worded voltage ranges. Rows missing a selected required parameter appear in the review filter and its count. In typed label/value rows other printed decimals help disambiguate grouping commas. Wrapped motor identifiers and multi-tier transformer schedules can still lose entire products. Scanned pages need browser OCR and are not scored."
    ],
    "changeGuide": [
      {
        "task": "Change a formula",
        "read": [
          "src/engine/sheet.ts",
          "tests/sheet.test.ts",
          "tests/fixtures/excel-crosscheck.json"
        ],
        "checks": [
          "npm test",
          "npm run typecheck"
        ],
        "rule": "Keep workbook parity; regenerate appropriate Excel fixtures if a source-workbook revision is explicitly authorized."
      },
      {
        "task": "Change import parsing",
        "read": [
          "src/import/load-list.ts",
          "src/ui/LoadList.tsx",
          "tests/load-list.test.ts"
        ],
        "rule": "Preserve malformed values for review and retain explicit units; test round-trip import/export."
      },
      {
        "task": "Change the export",
        "read": [
          "src/export/template.ts",
          "public/templates/cable-sizing.xlsx",
          "tests/sheet.test.ts"
        ],
        "rule": "Preserve template XML, OFFSET validations and all original lookup sheets, plus the live earth loop / short-circuit columns AP-BO, helpers BP-CP and the FaultData sheet."
      },
      {
        "task": "Change drums",
        "read": [
          "src/engine/drums.ts",
          "src/engine/procurement.ts",
          "src/ui/Drums.tsx",
          "src/ui/DrumSources.tsx",
          "src/ui/DrumVisual.tsx"
        ],
        "rule": "Test whole-run conservation, OD-specific overrides, bend radius, payload/lift and changes to linked products."
      },
      {
        "task": "Any change",
        "read": [
          "AGENTS.md",
          "spool-studio.dkg"
        ],
        "rule": "Use the graph to locate relevant files; read those files before editing. Update docs/project-knowledge.json when semantics change, run checks, refresh the DKG. Run tests/hardening.test.ts; any new file or text input needs size limits and a hostile-input test."
      },
      {
        "task": "Change the dashboard, issues, calculation panel or report",
        "read": [
          "src/ui/LoadList.tsx",
          "src/ui/Calculation.tsx",
          "src/ui/Report.tsx",
          "src/engine/issues.ts",
          "src/engine/explain.ts",
          "tests/upgrades.test.ts"
        ],
        "checks": [
          "npm run check"
        ],
        "rule": "Derive from sheet.ts results; keep cell references in Excel row numbers; keep print styles inside @media print."
      },
      {
        "task": "Change schematic import",
        "read": [
          "src/import/schematic.ts",
          "src/import/schematic-read.ts",
          "src/ui/Schematic.tsx",
          "tests/schematic.test.ts",
          "src/import/raster.ts",
          "src/import/drawing-ocr.ts",
          "tests/drawing.test.ts"
        ],
        "checks": [
          "npm test",
          "npm run check"
        ],
        "rule": "Keep extraction deterministic and value-preserving; record every worked-out value in inferred with a reason; keep limits and linear-time parsing; add a synthetic drawing test for each new layout or notation."
      },
      {
        "task": "Change the catalogue reader",
        "read": [
          "src/import/webpage.ts",
          "src/import/vocabulary.ts",
          "src/import/checks.ts",
          "src/import/parse.ts",
          "tests/equipment-reading.test.ts",
          "tests/catalogue-params.test.ts",
          "tests/checks.test.ts"
        ],
        "checks": [
          "npm test",
          "npm run bench"
        ],
        "rule": "Run the bench on the engineer's own confirmed datasheets in samples/bench before and after the change; tests use made-up sheets only, and real datasheets are never committed."
      }
    ]
  },
