      "role": "An engineer's arithmetic on a datasheet row (checkRow): a kVA rating over √3·U gives each side's current, kW over √3·U·cosφ (·η for shaft output) gives a load's current, kVA over kVA plus no-load and load losses gives efficiency at power factor 1 or 0.8, and a load's protection is at least its current. Sides (HV/LV, primary/secondary, input/output) come from parameter names; phases from the row or its Phases parameter, a supply above 250 V being three-phase. A relation that fails flags its values as doubt with the sum; withCheck and checkAll apply it to review rows; withTypes uses it to choose between tied values.",
      "exports": [
        "Check",
        "checkAll",
        "checkRow",
        "withCheck"
      ],
      "imports": [
