      "path": "src/import/rating-table.ts",
      "bytes": 43168,
      "sha256": "e76be3805f0d1fd403e9d581fee0acc1dd8121068a0471842a91f77a8c8264f5",
      "role": "Columns are named by vocabulary.ts in any listed language, checked against their values, and found from P = √3·U·I·η·cosφ when no heading is understood; type/series name = model, row-distinguishing code (product ID, frame) = configuration, title product name for size-only tables. Catalogue rating tables (one row per motor/pump/fan) read by column position from PDF item x/width: columns from overlapping numbers, stacked headings classified bottom-up (kW, hp, In at 400 V, efficiency/power factor at full load; starting current, torque, weight skipped), poles from speed or sub-headings, voltage/Hz/phase from the heading context. Rows are checked against P = √3·U·I·η·cosφ (In/Un flagged when they do not add up); a name column repeated down the table goes into the configuration, and every value keeps its page box for the review's page view. Drawn borders (rulesOf) keep a heading inside its own cell and stop values joining a column across a border. A load-point column (100 %, 75 %, 4/4) that no heading names takes its neighbour's efficiency or power-factor field, so a heading centred over 75 % still yields full-load values. With equipment types picked (catalogueFromTables types), each table is read for the type whose ticked parameters its columns give most: feedsOf gives every load-list-feeding parameter its column by nameScore (one column each, best first, efficiency/pf at full load only), else the vocabulary/P-formula column of the one quantity its label names; a table needs two parameters with columns and half the required ones, so breaker, DB, capacitor and other non-motor tables are read and motor-only rules apply only without types.",
