      "role": "Pure, deterministic schematic-to-load-list engine (no AI). DXF parser (TEXT/MTEXT/ATTRIB, binary/size guards, bounded MTEXT clean-up), glyph/word merging on shared baselines, readFacts (breaker A, poles/phase, kW/HP/W/kVA, PF, diversity, voltage incl. 400/230 pairs but not cable insulation ratings, cable type/cores/size/sets, run length, tags, board names, fed-from/feeds-to, spares, title-block words), circuit-schedule table detection (reuses detectColumns/toSheetRows plus cell rescue), single-line-diagram grouping around breaker ratings for column or row layouts with a proximity fallback, board ownership, From→To feeder chain, deduplication across drawings, inferred values with reasons, and limits (100k text items, 20k per page, 4k breakers per page, 200 pages, 2,000 candidates). Traced line work (from images or rendered PDF pages) gives one row per feeder: the busbar label (board tag first, within 7 text heights above or 15 left of its start) is From for drops and To for incomers; labels attach to the nearest feeder by distance from the nearest part of the text, with the far end counting 4 text heights closer and vertical text along the feeder preferred for the load name. Also reads US/MV notation (6-1/C 500 → 1C, 500 kcmil, 2 sets; 3/0 AWG; ft and miles to metres; MW, MVA), ETAP-style tags (TR:4, 3WTR:1, Bus A), transformer ratings into B, and treats a bare C16 as an MCB rating only on pages that mention MCBs or amps.",
