      "role": "Rating-table field vocabulary as data: words for kW, current, voltage, efficiency, power factor, speed, poles, type/series names, part codes, frame sizes and not-load-data columns in English, German, French, Spanish, Italian, Portuguese, Dutch, Polish, Turkish, Russian and Chinese, plus symbols and units matched as printed; fieldsIn scores a heading line (longest phrase first, abbreviations by prefix). nameScore matches any equipment type's parameter to a printed label three ways: by the quantity both name in any vocabulary word (Rated power for Rated output, FLA for Rated current) with every other word printed, by the parameter's own words (fuzzy OSA distance for OCR slips, bracketed words optional), or by a symbol printed (In, Ue, Icu; another symbol of the same quantity rejects); units must agree. namesQuantity, unitNames (kvar, kVA, lm name their quantity alone) and users' own units serve the readers. Words printed for one another (HV/high, LV/low, Specs/standard) are alike; a load point (75 % load, full load) is not part of a name while no-load stays one word; what follows \"at\" in a printed label is its condition and never makes it another parameter. A label the engineer taught by clicking its value (Param.labels) names its parameter before any other route.",
