      "role": "Vendor product web pages pasted from the browser or saved as .html: HTML to text (regex, never rendered), label/value pairs and comparison tables to catalogue proposals, HP to kW, checked with verify. Also reads PDF datasheets laid out as label/value columns (catalogueFromDatasheet): long labels match by their known start only with the field's unit, signal inputs and losses skipped, ligatures and wrapped labels rejoined, brand from label, title or copyright. With equipment types picked, a one-product sheet or page is read for each type (paramsOf: every ticked parameter, feeding or not, takes its best-named label, one value each, best first, full load preferred, part load only when the parameter is named at it, a unit like kvar printed once names its parameter, running-text lines split by looseOf); the product takes the type found most and its load list columns come only from that type's parameters, in the column's unit (W and hp as kW). A label split by a symbol in another font (\"Efficiency (\", \"ɳ\", \") at 100% Load\") is rejoined at its brackets; a power in kVA or kvar is never kW; columns the chosen type does not fill are cleared; each value read is boxed where it is printed (placeOn: the item on the line after its label). Lines are read with the section heading printed over them (HV side, Losses). Two labels naming a parameter equally with different values are settled by the row's sums (checks.ts). pickAt reads a value clicked in the review's page view and the label printed before it; placeOn boxes a value printed as several items.",
