        "reads merged title cells from a real XLSX and sizes the loads under their panel",
        "reads an equipment register with a worksheet per panel named in words",
        "keeps identical loads on different panels",
        "flags a load whose list In (A) is far from the calculated Ib, and reads 230 V as single-phase"
      ],
      "runtime": false
    },
    {
      "path": "tests/rating-table-params.test.ts",
      "bytes": 7972,
      "sha256": "7cc2a7c8148345fef8040f1b9bd79cf63d07dfb70ef9abda88a2db7821b9204d",
      "role": "Regression test or fixture.",
      "exports": [],
      "imports": [
        "../src/engine/equipment-types",
        "../src/import/parse",
        "../src/import/rating-table",
        "../src/import/vocabulary",
        "vitest"
      ],
      "tests": [
        "fills each catalogue-only parameter from its column, the row, or the title, and keeps the efficiency class in the series name",
        "reads nothing extra when no parameter is ticked",
        "does not take a section heading in capitals for the model",
        "recognises PDF ratio subscripts on a second line and distinguishes starting current from torque",
        "reads a starter range at the voltage over its kW column, past a picture label in the margin and a control supply",
        "gives each row the value of a cell drawn across several rows, and takes no section title for a heading or a name"
      ],
      "runtime": false
    },
    {
      "path": "tests/release.test.mjs",
      "bytes": 878,
      "sha256": "3678ceb05255b9869416e2bfa58ea10fd0963e4a5d901c9a4b26f07eb64d8641",
      "role": "Regression test or fixture.",
      "exports": [],
      "imports": [
        "../scripts/verify-vendor.mjs",
        "node:fs/promises",
        "node:os",
        "node:path",
        "vitest"
      ],
      "tests": [
        "keeps unlisted documents and linked files out of the static release"
      ],
      "runtime": false
    },
    {
      "path": "tests/schematic.test.ts",
      "bytes": 13029,
      "sha256": "2d3ecc180733148f5e1a0d81b2414a1f63374426d45eefc9cb5bddcb48f1c93a",
      "role": "Regression test or fixture.",
      "exports": [],
      "imports": [
        "../src/engine/sheet",
        "../src/engine/suggest",
        "../src/import/guard",
        "../src/import/schematic",
        "vitest"
      ],
      "tests": [
        "recognises protection, phases, cable and load annotations",
        "does not mistake ratings, wiring or titles for loads and voltages",
        "joins characters a PDF split on one baseline and keeps separate columns apart",
        "drops empty or non-finite items",
        "finds each outgoing circuit with its board, load, protection, cable and run",
        "reads a circuit schedule table and its board name",
        "links feeders so total voltage drop chains from the source",
        "marks every value that was worked out rather than read",
        "hands rows to the Cable Sizing sheet, which sizes every circuit",
        "reads a DB drawn with circuits running across the sheet",
        "reads schedule headers that wrap onto a second line, ignoring a note just above",
        "falls back to proximity when there is only one breaker",
        "reads text, MTEXT formatting and block attributes",
        "gives bare attribute numbers the unit their name implies",
        "rejects binary, foreign or damaged files with a clear message",
        "enforces the text-item limits",
        "stays fast on stacked, random and very long text",
        "keeps MTEXT clean-up linear and survives huge paragraph counts",
        "handles DXF text that tries to break the parser",
        "reads PNG, JPEG and WebP dimensions from the header alone"
      ],
      "runtime": false
    },
    {
      "path": "tests/serial-rows.test.ts",
      "bytes": 2606,
      "sha256": "d357145862b7cb7bc9f91a3ffe89884067729c50cdff73a775da1463d38b0719",
      "role": "Regression test or fixture.",
      "exports": [],
      "imports": [
        "../src/import/equipment",
        "../src/import/load-list",
        "exceljs",
        "vitest"
      ],
      "tests": [
        "takes the numbered rows as the items and reads each value from its column"
      ],
      "runtime": false
    },
    {
      "path": "tests/sheet.test.ts",
      "bytes": 12703,
      "sha256": "e986b0f2044385027e6153454b470ae489318002169366bc1771f8937839120f",
      "role": "Regression test or fixture.",
      "exports": [],
      "imports": [
        "../src/engine/sheet",
        "../src/engine/suggest",
        "../src/export/template",
        "../src/import/load-list",
        "./fixtures/excel-crosscheck.json",
        "./fixtures/excel-fault-crosscheck.json",
        "jszip",
        "node:fs",
        "vitest"
      ],
      "tests": [
        "matches the values Microsoft Excel calculated for 260 rows of the supplied workbook",
        "matches Excel for 165 TN-S and TT circuits of the step08 earth fault loop, RCD, CPC, breaking capacity and short-circuit columns",
        "applies the workbook blank rules: diversity 1, THD 0, factors 1 and one cable",
        "suggests the smallest size meeting Ib ≤ In ≤ Iz and the VD limit",
        "adds the upstream feeder total VD only when From is filled, as the workbook does",
        "checks motor starting VD: total VD at From plus the cable VD at the starting current, as the step09 workbook does",
        "narrows dropdowns left to right and turns stale picks red",
        "reports temperatures and soil beyond the catalogue tables as out of range",
        "fills blanks with a standard protection rating, the list defaults and a passing size",
        "never overwrites a typed value and adds parallel cables when one cable cannot carry the load",
        "sizes feeders before the circuits they supply so total VD is respected",
        "re-sizes a circuit from its cache only when its feeder is unchanged",
        "exports one Cable Sizing sheet per panel, each with its own loads, filter and header notes",
        "keeps a list where a row feeds another panel on one sheet, so Excel can chain total VD",
        "makes Excel-safe, unique sheet names",
        "types inputs into the template and keeps its formulas live",
        "extends formulas, dropdowns and colour rules past the template rows for long lists"
      ],
      "runtime": false
    },
    {
      "path": "tests/upgrades.test.ts",
      "bytes": 4354,
      "sha256": "c8063942c1fda3e750a68f164fc24cd43b581ee74cfc6d13b2736edb71633331",
      "role": "Regression test or fixture.",
      "exports": [],
      "imports": [
        "../src/engine/explain",
        "../src/engine/issues",
        "../src/engine/sheet",
        "../src/import/guard",
        "../src/ui/state",
        "node:fs",
        "vitest"
      ],
      "tests": [
        "ranks every size with the same tests as the Suggested Cable Size column",
        "includes the upstream total VD in every step and follows the feeder chain from the source",
        "reports failures, duplicates, chain breaks and missing inputs, errors first",
        "accepts the workbook template and rejects non-zips and decompression bombs",
        "restores whole-project snapshots and groups typing in one cell",
        "starts from a neutral, empty workspace in one undoable step"
      ],
      "runtime": false
    },
